{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/990731-custom-totems","id":990731,"title":"Custom Totems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-20T18:26:47-07:00","id":990731,"title":"Custom Totems","content":"Being a long term fan of Forsaken, I always disappointed to find that Apocalypse's totems were narrowed down into a list, and a list that I personally felt was wildly unbalanced. So, I set out to make rules for creating custom totems. Please note that I'm coming at this from a 20th Anniversary perspective.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 1: Totem Concept. </b><br /> The players and storyteller work together to choose and flesh out their totem. It could be from the core, like Owl, or something entirely new, like Firebird or Basilisk.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 2. Buy Traits</b><br /> Players spend their combined totem points on totem benefits. We'll use the Freebie Points chart for costs. The storyteller has the final say if a totem bonuses' are acceptable.<br /> <br /> Attribute Bonus -- 5<br /> Ability Bonus -- 2<br /> -1 Difficulty to X Rolls -- 3<br /> Rage -- 1<br /> Willpower -- 1<br /> Gnosis -- 2<br /> Gifts/Powers* -- 7<br /> <br /> *Includes powers like Chimera's umbra disguises or Uktena's XP bonuses.<br /> <br /> The totem bonus' can only be bought at character creation/when the totem bonds with the pack. After that, extra totem points go into improving the totem as listed in the core book.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 3. Final Touches</b><br /> Work out the totems ban, and if it would give any Renown boost.<br /> <br /> Thoughts and suggestions? I'm still unsure with how to deal with Pack Traits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12455-keter","name":"Keter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12455_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T18:46:03-07:00","id":990741,"title":"","content":"Might be lazy on my part, but I would be more inclined to slightly tweak or re-skin an existing totem rather than make it a point buy system. I would rather keep some of the backbone of what White Wolf originally provided rather than strip it down and start over from the ground up. If someone wanted to have Humming Bird as a totem but were in an Old-World setting, I would allow them to use another creature with fast reaction time instead (while using the rules for Humming Bird as appropriate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-21-2016, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T00:22:23-07:00","id":990834,"title":"","content":"While reskins and the massive extant Rev./W20 Totem list can cover most things conceptually, it doesn't really deal with the extant list being really mechanically weird.<br /> <br /> There's so many cool Totems conceptually that people never take because they suck (usually either are silly expensive for what they give, or the bans are virtually unplayable), or STs don't allow them because they're so good (the opposite).<br /> <br /> I've been playing WtA for ~20 years now from normal TT, to large games with a dozen PC packs involved. Of all the Totems printed, I can't think of more than two dozen I've actually seen used. That to me indicates that the giant list approach really isn't the right way to go.<br /> <br /> From a game design perspective, it's also a lot less page space to have a build your own Totem section than a massive list that doesn't follow a recognizable formula to base your own on, and it makes any example Totems future writers want to put in the books faster to create because they have a built in guide in how to do so.<br /> <br /> So to me, a well designed build your own Totem offers two important things:<br /> <br /> 1) Increases the diversity of Totems in play, because it ensures that players can focus on the conceptual appropriateness of the Totem instead of worrying about the mechanical value of them. This also has an interesting side benefit that different Totem avatar spirits can have different expressions of the same core Totem instead of granting the same benefits with the variations only coming from how the players spend extra Totem points. So a pack following Eagle operating out of a major breeding ground for local eagles can have a spirit that cares more about protecting that breeding ground and is more centered on the physical world, while a different pack following Eagle might be working with a much more symbolic eagle-spirit with an appropriate change in attitude and stats.<br /> <br /> 2) Makes the game more enjoyable because you can just get the Totem that you want instead of hunting for a Totem that kind of fits, and trying to reskin and adjust it until it fits. Creating a Totem together as a group helps the players build the pack together (since the Totem is the core of the pack) and is well worth the time of fiddling with the point buy process compared to hunting for the right Totem from a big list. It also avoids things like, &quot;I want to play a Philodox, no Honor penalty Totems,&quot; keeping the pack away from otherwise cool Totems because you can just build a version of Fox or Butterfly that doesn't have that issue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}